#12900
diary dissolution~
the Diary of Dissolutionment~
A leather-bound book is here, with its pages strewn chaotically about.~
~
14 e ao 0
0 0 0 0 0
5 3 300 100 0 1
E
diary dissolution~
It is a ragged diary - obviously it's seen better days. There are several
entries written within, but the only semi-legible ones are the first and
second pages.
~
E
first~
   It has now been eleven days since the ruthless members of the Liu'she
Ch'uan Tong have imprisoned me. It all started when I noticed peculiar
disappearences of goods and thefts of the sacred offerings at the temple
left by the whole-hearted citizens of Kir-Oshi. I decided to launch an
investigation to see if I could put an end to these loathsome happenings.
What an error I have made.
   I searched throughout the entire city... But alas, I was unable to find
any information of value. I spoke with the dirty and stinking sailors and
pirates passing through the harbor; and met a mysterious merchant passing
through who told me that the members of the Liu'she Ch'uan Tong criminal
orginization have been making enormous amounts of profit from the trade of
theft and smuggling. 
~
E
second~
   I began to ask around town, but could not receive any straightforward
answer as to the location of the Tong hideout. While I was taking a break
from the investigation drinking at the local Bars Crossed Tavern, I met
a beautiful young lady who claimed she was an ex-member of the notorious
gang. We began to talk whilst drinking expensive ale, and I managed to get
quite drunk off of the accursed necture.
   The next morning, I awoke chained to a filthy ship, with mere scraps of
food and dirty water to accompany me. Apparently this woman poisoned the
ale that I drank and imprisoned me for snooping around. There is no hope
now, save for an adventurer stumbling onto my floating prison and saving me
before I meet my end.
~
