~
8 0 ao 0
0 0 0 0 0
5 3 1000 75 0 1
E
ivory tusk~
Carved into it is a scene with hundreds of tiny figures smaller than
a pea. Looking closely, the people are all clothed in ceremonious
garb. The craftsmanship is absolutely exquisite; it must have taken
the artist decades to produce such a fine piece. It still retains the
basic shape of a tusk however - that being a slightly curved, off-white
enamel. The Tong probably make heaps of money off of items like this on
a daily basis.
~
#12915
disturbing painting~
a painting~
A disturbing painting hangs on the wall, half hidden by the other canvases.~
~
15 e 0 0
200 15 12916 0 0
1 3 0 100 0 1
E
disturbing painting~
It is a superb and haunting watercolor brush painting of an old sage identified
as Seiji. The actual &Wframe&n looks older than the painting itself, as evidenced
by the dust around the worn edges. It is painted on a fine grade of rice
paper - four sheets that have been joined to a single large sheet. You are
particularly taken with the solemn, but gentle expression of this ancient wise
man, noticing also how cleverly the artist portrayed the diaphonous nature of
the head scarf as the ears show through it. Very strong rhythmic strokes of the
brush skillfully set forth the head scarf. Yet the face - in particular the sad
contemplative eyes and the flowing beard - are done in wonderful detail. One
small touch of red on the handle of the whisk makes a dramatic contrast to the
overall somber colors of tans and grays. There is a strange, symbolic &Wsignature&n
in the right hand corner of the painting.
~
E
signature~
It is a four character signature with a miniature seal placed in the bottom
right hand corner of the painting. The seal in particular is a work of
exquisite art: a golden, snake-like dragon - the Liu'she Ch'uan Tong insignia.
You wonder as to the origins of this painting ... Was it made as a gift for
the Tong? Or did an artist from within the orginization paint it? It is also
quite possible that a lowly member of the Tong came across this ancient relic
during his scheming smuggling operations. The answer seems hidden within the
sage's sad, worn eyes.
~
E
frame~
The frame of the painting is made of solid gold. It is ornately carved and, by
the dust which covers it, you are able to ascertain that it is very old indeed.
~
